## 4. Dex

Add the relay's static client to Dex's configuration, with its one redirect URI:

```yaml
staticClients:
  - id: {{.ClientID}}
    name: patchy previews
    secretEnv: {{.SecretEnv}}
    redirectURIs:
      - https://{{.SignIn}}/dex/callback
```

Give Dex the secret in that environment variable from the Secret in its namespace (with Dex's Helm chart:
`envVars: [{name: {{.SecretEnv}}, valueFrom: {secretKeyRef: {name: {{.DexSecret}}, key: {{.DexSecretKey}}}}}]`),
then roll Dex:

```sh
kubectl apply -f {{.DexSecretFile}}
```

## 5. TLS

{{if .Certificate -}}
```sh
kubectl apply -f {{.CertificateFile}}
kubectl -n {{.Namespace}} wait certificate/{{.CertificateName}} --for=condition=Ready --timeout=10m
```

Both Ingresses name its Secret, `{{.CertificateSecret}}`. Put no `cert-manager.io/*issuer` annotation on either: a
second Certificate for the same Secret would fight this one.
{{- else if .Route -}}
Your Gateway `{{.GatewayNamespace}}/{{.GatewayName}}` terminates TLS. Give it one HTTPS listener for `*.{{.Suffix}}`
{{- if .GatewaySection}} (the listener `{{.GatewaySection}}` the previews' route names){{end}} and one for
`{{.SignIn}}`, each with a certificate (the wildcard never covers the sign-in host), and allow routes from namespace
`{{.Namespace}}`. Then route the sign-in host to the gateway:

```sh
kubectl apply -f {{.SignInRouteFile}}
```
{{- else -}}
The edge terminates TLS: it must hold a certificate for `*.{{.Suffix}}` and one for `{{.SignIn}}` (the wildcard never
covers the sign-in host).
{{- if eq .Platform "eks"}} Both Ingresses take the chart's edge class: set `edgeIngressClass.create: true` in your
values if it is not already, and add the two ACM certificates' ARNs to `edgeIngressClass.certificateARNs` (the ALB
picks one by SNI).{{end}}
{{- end}}

## 6. Install

```sh
kubectl apply -f {{.RelaySecretFile}}
helm upgrade {{.Release}} {{.ChartRef}} -n {{.Namespace}}{{if .ChartVersion}} --version {{.ChartVersion}}{{end}} \
  -f <your values> -f {{.ValuesFile}}
```

One upgrade: the gateway needs no permit stage. `previewController.config.apiServerCIDR: {{.APIServerCIDR}}`
{{- if eq .APIServerCIDR "auto"}} is looked up at render time, so it needs `helm upgrade` against the cluster (not
`helm template` or a GitOps render, which must set the kubernetes Service's `/32` instead){{else}} is the API server
address the preview-controller may reach{{end}}.

## 7. DNS

Point two records at the edge's address:

- `*.{{.Suffix}}`
- `{{.SignIn}}`

{{if .Route -}}
The address is your Gateway's (`kubectl -n {{.GatewayNamespace}} get gateway {{.GatewayName}}`). An HTTPRoute
publishes no address of its own, so also set `previewAuth.gateway.publishedAddresses` to it in your values for
`patchy check previews`.
{{- else -}}
The address is the Ingress controller's load balancer (`kubectl -n {{.Namespace}} get ingress {{.GatewayService}}`
once it is admitted). `previewAuth.gateway.forwardedHops: 1` holds when the controller sees the client's address
(its Service has `externalTrafficPolicy: Local`, or it trusts the PROXY protocol); behind a cloud L7 load balancer
that also appends `X-Forwarded-For`, it is 2.
{{- end}}

## 8. Check

```sh
patchy check previews -n {{.Namespace}}
```

Every line should PASS before the first intent's preview is opened.

## Rolling back

In reverse order, all by deletion:

1. Set `previewAuth.gateway.enabled: false` (or `preview.enabled: false`) and run the same `helm upgrade`.
{{- if .Certificate}}
2. `kubectl delete -f {{.CertificateFile}}`
{{- else if .Route}}
2. `kubectl delete -f {{.SignInRouteFile}}`
{{- else}}
2. Remove the certificates from the edge, if nothing else uses them.
{{- end}}
3. Remove the two DNS records.
4. Remove the static client from Dex, and delete the Secrets (`kubectl delete -f secrets/`).
5. Delete what the chart keeps on uninstall, as `docs/intents/preview-sign-in.md` lists it.
